{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And you shall not set up a pillar for yourself.</b> As for a pillar for idolatry — and the proof is that He only hated a pillar that is not for idolatry — it is not prohibited, and the faithful witness is in the section of Jacob's sending [Genesis 31]."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {0 "The syntax of the second clause is difficult; read hyper-literally: 'and the proof is that [if] He only hated a pillar that is not for idolatry, it is not prohibited.' The logic and the referent of 'faithful witness' are left cryptic as per discipline."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:44.855753133Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}